---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import Arrow from './Arrow.astro';

const compiledSql = readFileSync(resolve('public/examples/renal_measurements.postgresql.sql'), 'utf8');
const ruleExcerpt = `// Summarise a patient's recorded measurements
egfr_latest => eadv.lab_bld_egfr.val.last();
egfr_lowest => eadv.lab_bld_egfr.val.min();`;
const sqlExcerpt = `WITH egfr_history AS (
  SELECT eid, val,
    MIN(val::numeric) OVER (
      PARTITION BY eid
    ) AS egfr_lowest,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
      PARTITION BY eid ORDER BY dt DESC
    ) AS observation_order
  FROM eadv
  WHERE att = 'lab_bld_egfr'
)
SELECT eid,
  val AS egfr_latest,
  egfr_lowest
FROM egfr_history
WHERE observation_order = 1;`;
---

<section id="language" class="language shell" aria-labelledby="language-heading">
  <div class="language-introduction">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">02 — The language</p><h2 id="language-heading">A small definition.<br /><em>A clearer intention.</em></h2></div>
    <p>Picorules began by making clinical calculations easier to maintain in a database. Its compact definitions now also run in JavaScript, while keeping the clinical question in view.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="comparison">
    <div class="code-panel">
      <div class="panel-heading"><span class="eyebrow">SQL</span><span>Retrieval equivalent</span></div>
      <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="SQL retrieval example"><code>{sqlExcerpt}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="code-panel definition-panel">
      <div class="panel-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Picorules</span><span>renal_measurements.prb · excerpt</span></div>
      <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Picorules retrieval example"><code>{ruleExcerpt}</code></pre>
      <div class="definition-note">
        <h3>Two questions, made explicit.</h3>
        <p>What is the latest recorded eGFR? What is the lowest? These summaries are reusable constructs that can contribute to a larger phenotype definition.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/examples/renal_measurements.prb" download>Get the complete ruleblock <Arrow /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="example-caption">An observation-summary example, with no disease classification. The SQL shows the retrieval operation; the compiler also supplies the surrounding ruleblock and output structure.</p>
  <details class="compiled-output">
    <summary>Inspect the actual compiler output <span>PostgreSQL</span></summary>
    <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Complete compiled PostgreSQL example"><code>{compiledSql}</code></pre>
    <a class="text-link" href="/examples/renal_measurements.postgresql.sql" download>Download the SQL <Arrow /></a>
  </details>
  <div class="language-notes">
    <div><h3>History, made usable.</h3><p>Select the latest result, summarise an interval, or follow change over time. Work with dated observations through the EADV model.</p><a href="/docs/functions-reference/">Explore the functions →</a></div>
    <div><h3>Definitions that compose.</h3><p>Reuse named outputs from other ruleblocks. Build richer clinical descriptions from smaller, explicit constructs.</p><a href="/docs/language-reference/#cross-ruleblock-binding">Explore composition →</a></div>
    <div><h3>Reasoning beside the rule.</h3><p>Keep descriptions, citation keys, and output labels alongside the definition with documentation and attribute directives.</p><a href="/docs/language-reference/#doc">Explore documentation →</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
